
# Project 04 - Container Security Hardening

Campus Student Services System

## Project Overview

This project explores container security hardening using Docker Compose, Apache HTTPD and PostgreSQL within a simulated campus student services environment.

The project focuses on Linux capability management, least-privilege configuration, privilege escalation prevention, network segmentation, resource management, persistent storage and database disaster recovery.

## Technical Objectives

- Deploy Apache HTTPD and PostgreSQL containers.
- Apply the principle of least privilege.
- Disable privileged container execution.
- Remove unnecessary Linux capabilities.
- Prevent additional privilege acquisition.
- Restore only necessary capabilities when justified.
- Restrict unnecessary host filesystem access.
- Implement frontend and backend network segmentation.
- Maintain persistent database storage.
- Perform database backup and restoration.

